        "created_at": "2017-08-03T20:26:11.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>So, this just came up while I am playing my first 2 spirit solo game.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>I goofed and Ocean doesn't have the energy to pay for both the cards I want to play this turn, however, River is going to be playing a card to give Ocean energy this turn. As I can determine the order and both things are fast, I can gain the energy before I activate the card.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>My question, is that a legal move? Can you play a card you cannot afford if you will gain the energy to use it before the card activates? And, if you do play such a card, but something happens and you cannot gain the energy, what happens?</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>My understanding is that you have to assign the energy when you play the cards, but is this incorrect?</p>",
        "post_number": 1,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:49:53.289Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
        "quote_count": 0,
        "incoming_link_count": 85,
        "reads": 2,
        "readers_count": 1,
        "score": 415.4,
